diff --git a/docs/source/user_guide/building_doc/building_fabric.md b/docs/source/user_guide/building_doc/building_fabric.md
index 033d269..fa4e822 100644
--- a/docs/source/user_guide/building_doc/building_fabric.md
+++ b/docs/source/user_guide/building_doc/building_fabric.md
@@ -27,6 +27,12 @@ routing channels must match the neighboring core tile. The default example
 fabric keeps its existing `RAM_IO` east edge, so creating a project does not
 change the example layout automatically.
 
+New projects also include an `E_IO` east-boundary IO tile under `Tile/E_IO`.
+It is the east-side mirror of `W_IO` and contains two bidirectional IO BELs,
+with the prefixes `A_` and `B_`. Place it only on east-edge rows whose W1, W2,
+WW4, and W6 channels match the adjacent core tile. Registering the tile does
+not replace the default example's `RAM_IO` east edge automatically.
+
 (fabulous-directory)=
 ### The .FABulous directory
 
